{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMVGJdgPvdbUS1pczziHqX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Task\n3\ttype: schema\n4\tentity: Task\n5\tversion: 1\n6\tschema:\n7\t  description: string, what needs to be done\n8\t  status?(enum, current state): [active, blocked, done, abandoned]\n9\t  assigned_to?: string, who is working on this\n10\t  steps?(array): string, ordered steps to complete\n11\t  current_step?: integer, which step number we're on (1-indexed)\n12\t  context?: string, key context needed to resume after memory loss\n13\t  started?: string, when work began\n14\t  completed?: string, when work finished\n15\t  blockers?(array): string, what's preventing progress\n16\t  parent_task?: Task, parent task if this is a subtask\n17\tsettings:\n18\t  validation: warn\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t# Task\n22\t\n23\tA **Task** is work-in-progress tracked as a note, so it survives context\n24\tcompaction and shows up in the next session's brief. This schema is the same one\n25\tthe framework-agnostic [`memory-tasks`](https://github.com/basicmachines-co/basic-memory/tree/main/skills/memory-tasks)\n26\tskill defines — kept identical here so the plugin and the skill agree on the\n27\tshape. For the full task workflow (creating, updating, completing), use that\n28\tskill.\n29\t\n30\tTasks are found by the SessionStart hook via structured recall:\n31\t`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"task\", \"status\": \"active\"})`.\n32\t\n33\t## Frontmatter vs observations\n34\t\n35\tPut queryable fields (`status`, `priority`, `current_step`) in frontmatter so\n36\t`filters` can find them, and mirror them as `- [status] active`\n37\tobservations so `bm_schema(command=\"validate\")` sees them. `note_type=\"Task\"` is stored as\n38\tlowercase `task` in frontmatter, so search with `note_types=[\"task\"]`.\n39\tValidation is `warn` — advisory, never blocking.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a2f24c1-9e25-487b-99d5-6ab33f3a7dc3","uuid":"f6779141-ef8e-48e0-8829-3e52c2ea83fc","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:15:25.637Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/_temp/basic-memory/plugins/claude-code/schemas/task.md","content":"---\ntitle: Task\ntype: schema\nentity: Task\nversion: 1\nschema:\n  description: string, what needs to be done\n  status?(enum, current state): [active, blocked, done, abandoned]\n  assigned_to?: string, who is working on this\n  steps?(array): string, ordered steps to complete\n  current_step?: integer, which step number we're on (1-indexed)\n  context?: string, key context needed to resume after memory loss\n  started?: string, when work began\n  completed?: string, when work finished\n  blockers?(array): string, what's preventing progress\n  parent_task?: Task, parent task if this is a subtask\nsettings:\n  validation: warn\n---\n\n# Task\n\nA **Task** is work-in-progress tracked as a note, so it survives context\ncompaction and shows up in the next session's brief. This schema is the same one\nthe framework-agnostic [`memory-tasks`](https://github.com/basicmachines-co/basic-memory/tree/main/skills/memory-tasks)\nskill defines — kept identical here so the plugin and the skill agree on the\nshape. For the full task workflow (creating, updating, completing), use that\nskill.\n\nTasks are found by the SessionStart hook via structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"task\", \"status\": \"active\"})`.\n\n## Frontmatter vs observations\n\nPut queryable fields (`status`, `priority`, `current_step`) in frontmatter so\n`filters` can find them, and mirror them as `- [status] active`\nobservations so `bm_schema(command=\"validate\")` sees them. `note_type=\"Task\"` is stored as\nlowercase `task` in frontmatter, so search with `note_types=[\"task\"]`.\nValidation is `warn` — advisory, never blocking.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RMVGJdgPvdbUS1pczziHqX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
